    "title": "Fishtown Music Venues: A Guide to the Neighborhood's Stages - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tom Beck ,\n13 hours ago Fishtown takes its name from the commercial shad fishing that once defined it, and it grew up as a blue-collar, industrial neighborhood just northeast of Center City. The warehouses and rowhomes that made it a working district now hold some of Philadelphia's busiest rooms for live music. This guide covers the main stages, the age rules at each, and how to get in and out without a car. It draws on Visit Philadelphia's neighborhood guide and Philadelphia Magazine's venue roundup, so confirm age policies on each venue's calendar before buying tickets. Read full article",
